## Observations

- On this machine the CPU (6 threads) is faster than the iGPU for this model, both for generation and prompt processing.
- Both setups are very consistent: run-to-run spread is under 1%.
- Even with temperature 0 and a fixed seed, the two backends produced **different output**. The CPU finished naturally at 387 tokens, while every iGPU run hit the 400-token cap. So the total-time figures aren't a perfect like-for-like comparison. Tokens/s is the fairer number to compare.

